Thanks for the extra screenshots — they tell me two things:
	1.	The strftime issue is solved (no more errors about weblogic.time).
	2.	Now you’re hitting:

NameError: json

at the very end of your export_dev.py.

That means WLST’s Jython couldn’t import json. Some WLST distributions (especially 12.1/12.2) bundle an old Jython without the json module.

⸻

✅ Fix: fallback to simplejson

At the very top of your script, replace your import json with this:

try:
    import json
except ImportError:
    try:
        import simplejson as json
    except ImportError:
        # last resort: write a very basic JSON dumper
        def dumps(obj, indent=None, sort_keys=False):
            import repr
            return repr.repr(obj)
        class DummyJson:
            def dumps(self, o, indent=None, sort_keys=False): return dumps(o, indent, sort_keys)
        json = DummyJson()

This way:
	•	If json is available → use it.
	•	If not → fall back to simplejson (some Oracle homes ship it).
	•	If neither exists → crude dumper just so your script won’t crash.

